---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const post = {
 title: 'Custom Safety Vests: ANSI 107 Compliance and Where to Place Logos',
 description:
 'How employers can review garment classification, product documentation, and manufacturer approval before decorating high-visibility safety vests.',
 category: 'Compliance',
 readTime: '7 min read',
 date: 'May 9, 2026',
 isoDate: '2026-05-09',
 image: '/images/generated/service-screen-printing.jpg',
 slug: 'custom-safety-vests-ansi-compliance',
}

const faqs = [
 { q: 'Can you put a logo on an ANSI 107 safety vest?', a: 'Only after reviewing the exact garment and proposed decoration. Your employer selects the required performance class. The garment manufacturer should approve the method, size, and placement in writing.' },
 { q: 'What is the size limit for a logo on a hi-vis vest?', a: 'Do not use one universal size limit. Available background and reflective areas vary by garment, class, size, and current standard. Use the exact product documentation and a scaled proof.' },
 { q: 'Can decoration affect ANSI compliance on a safety vest?', a: 'Yes. Decoration can affect required background or reflective areas. Review the complete decorated garment with the employer, manufacturer, and safety lead before use.' },
 { q: 'Where on a safety vest can I put my company logo?', a: 'Placement is product specific. Start with the manufacturer\'s current decoration guide. Keep required reflective material and product labels unobstructed.' },
 { q: 'Can you embroider on a safety vest?', a: 'It depends on the exact garment. Embroidery adds thread, backing, and needle penetrations. Obtain manufacturer approval for the proposed materials and location.' },
 { q: 'What is the difference between Class 2 and Class 3 decoration planning?', a: 'Each class and garment design provides a different arrangement of background and reflective material. The employer selects the class from its hazard assessment. Then the manufacturer reviews the decoration plan.' },
 { q: 'Where can I get custom safety vests in Las Vegas?', a: 'Bighorn Threads coordinates selected safety vests and approved decoration through production partners. Your employer selects the required class. The garment manufacturer must approve the decoration method and placement.' },
]

const schema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@graph': [
 { '@type': 'Article', headline: post.title, description: post.description, image: `https://bighornthreads.com${post.image}`, datePublished: post.isoDate, dateModified: '2026-08-21', author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/images/logos/bighorn-logo-color.png' } }, mainEntityOfPage: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` },
 { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/blog/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: post.title, item: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` }] },
 { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
 ],
}

const speakableSchema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@type': 'WebPage',
 url: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`,
 name: post.title,
 speakable: {
  '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification',
  cssSelector: ['h1', '.speakable-answer'],
 },
}
---

<BaseLayout title={post.title} description={post.description} canonical={`https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`} ogImage={post.image} type="article" publishedDate={post.isoDate}>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(speakableSchema)} />
 <article class="bg-concrete">
 <header class="border-b border-hairline bg-paper">
 <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-20 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 lg:px-8">
 <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-ash" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-700">Home</a><span class="px-2">/</span><a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-gold-700">Blog</a></nav>
 <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">{post.category}</span>
 <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{post.title}</h1>
 <p class="mb-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-ash">A practical guide to reviewing an ANSI/ISEA 107 garment before adding a logo.</p>
 <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-hairline pt-6 font-mono text-sm text-ash"><span class="text-gold-600">Bighorn Threads Team</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span>{post.readTime}</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><time datetime={post.isoDate}>{post.date}</time></div>
 </div>
 </header>
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><img src={post.image} alt="Representative high-visibility garment shown for product and decoration planning" width="1200" height="675" loading="eager" class="w-full border border-hairline object-cover" /></div>
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

 <aside class="mb-10 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7">
 <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">Quick Answer</p>
 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-xl speakable-answer">Your employer selects the required high-visibility garment from its hazard assessment. Before decoration, verify the exact product, current standard, labels, and manufacturer instructions. Obtain written approval for the proposed method and placement.</p>
 </aside>

 <h2 id="why-rules" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Why Decoration Rules Matter on Safety Vests</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">High-visibility garments use background and reflective materials as a system. Decoration can cover or interrupt those materials. Review the complete finished garment.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><a href="https://safetyequipment.org/standards/ansi-isea-107/" rel="noopener" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">ANSI/ISEA 107</a> addresses high-visibility safety apparel. Applicable requirements can also come from the employer, project owner, agency, or contract. Confirm the current requirements for the actual work.</p>

 <h2 id="size-limit" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Measure the Exact Garment</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Do not apply a universal logo cap to every vest. Build a scaled proof for the exact style and size. Review each placement against current product documentation:</p>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>Identify the garment manufacturer, model, size, type, and class.</li>
 <li>Map all background and reflective material on the finished garment.</li>
 <li>Add every logo, name, badge, and identifier to one proof.</li>
 <li>Request written manufacturer and employer approval before production.</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Larger back graphics and multi-placement programs need extra review. Garment sizes can also change the available area.</p>

 <h2 id="placement" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Placements to Review</h2>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Front placements</h3>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Left chest panel.</strong> Review a proposed company logo against the exact garment.</li>
 <li><strong>Right chest panel.</strong> Review employee names or department identifiers the same way.</li>
 </ul>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Back placements</h3>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Back yoke.</strong> Confirm available background and clearance from reflective material.</li>
 <li><strong>Lower rear panel.</strong> Confirm the proposed identifier does not obstruct required material or labels.</li>
 </ul>

 <h3 class="mt-8 mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold">Avoid</h3>
 <ul class="mb-6 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>Any placement that covers, crosses, or obstructs retroreflective tape</li>
 <li>Oversized back logos that consume the entire back panel non-retroreflective area</li>
 <li>Decoration on the retroreflective stripes themselves</li>
 </ul>

 <h2 id="embroidery-vs-print" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Embroidery vs Screen Printing on Safety Vests</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><strong>Embroidery</strong> adds thread, backing, and needle penetrations. Ask the garment manufacturer to approve those materials and the proposed placement.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><strong>Screen printing</strong> adds ink and a curing process. Confirm ink compatibility, curing limits, size, and placement with the garment manufacturer.</p>

 <h2 id="class-2-vs-3" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Class 2 vs Class 3 Decoration Differences</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><strong>Class 2</strong> garments can use different designs and material layouts. Review the exact label, style, size, and product documentation.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal"><strong>Class 3</strong> garments can also use different configurations. Do not transfer a decoration proof from another class or garment without a new review.</p>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">For deeper context on choosing between Class 2 and Class 3, see <a href="/blog/ansi-107-class-2-vs-class-3-hi-vis-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">ANSI 107 Class 2 vs Class 3 hi-vis</a>.</p>

 <h2 id="ordering" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">How to Order Custom Safety Vests</h2>
 <p class="mb-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">See our <a href="/custom-safety-vests-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-600 underline decoration-gold-600/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-gold-600">custom safety vests Las Vegas</a> page for available options. Confirm availability and terms in your written quote. When building your order:</p>
 <ol class="mb-6 list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li><strong>Specify the class.</strong> Use the employer's hazard assessment and project documents.</li>
 <li><strong>Confirm the product.</strong> Record the manufacturer, model, size range, color, and current classification.</li>
 <li><strong>Plan decoration.</strong> List every placement, material, and finished size.</li>
 <li><strong>Obtain approval.</strong> Ask the manufacturer and employer to approve the complete proof.</li>
 <li><strong>Confirm terms.</strong> Put quantity, sizing, availability, pricing, and timing in the written quote.</li>
 </ol>

 <div class="mt-12 border border-hairline bg-gold-500/5 p-7 sm:p-9">
 <h2 class="mb-3 font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Custom ANSI 107 safety vests in Las Vegas</h2>
<p class="mb-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Bighorn Threads coordinates selected safety vests and approved decoration through production partners. Your employer selects the required class. The garment manufacturer must approve logo methods and placement.</p>
 <a href="/safety-compliance/" class="inline-flex min-h-[48px] items-center gap-2 bg-gold-500 px-7 py-3 text-base font-bold text-charcoal transition-all hover:bg-gold-600">See Safety & Compliance →</a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
